_L6 = [("Friend", "Mare, kailangan ko ng payo mo, ’yung hipag ko kasi ander sa akin sa trabaho. Bale bisor niya ako. Palagi siya kasing late dumating sa umaga. Nung tinanong ko kung bakit, sabi niya traffic daw, tapos nung sumunod, may banggaan daw. Tapos nung isang linggo may sakit daw ang bunso niyang anak. Mabait naman siya kaya lang lagi talagang late. Hindi ko alam kung paano ko pagsasabihan kasi, alam mo na, asawa ’yun ng kuya ko. Baka kasi isipan niya namemersonal ako. Ano ang gagawin ko?", "Mare, I need your advice. My sister-in-law is under me at work. So I am her supervisor. She is always late in the morning. When I asked why, she said traffic, then the next time, a collision. Then last week, her youngest child was sick. She is nice, but she is really always late. I do not know how to tell her because, you know, she is my older brother’s wife. She might think I am taking things personally. What should I do?")]
_L7 = [("Speaker 1", "O, ano’ng nangyari sayo at mukha kang Biyernes Santo. Hindi ba ka-po-promote mo lang sa trabaho, dapat masaya ka.", "Well, what happened to you that you look like Good Friday. Weren’t you just promoted at work, you should be happy."), ("Speaker 2", "’Yan nga po e, dahil sa promotion ko na ’yan. May utak talangka kasi sa opisina namin. Ang daming naiinggit. Ang sabi, kaya lang daw ako na-promote dahil magkaibigan ang boss ko at si Tatay. Oo, totoong magkaibigan sila, masama ba ’yun? Pero itong pag-po-promote sa akin, pinaghirapan ko ito. Ginagawa ko nang tama at sa oras ang trabahong ibinibigay sa akin. Pati nga dito sa bahay dinadala ko pa ang trabaho ko. Ang sakit nilang magsalita.", "That is it, it is because of that promotion. There is a crab mentality in our office. Many are envious. They said I was promoted only because my boss and Tatay are friends. Yes, it is true they are friends, is that bad? But this promotion, I worked hard for it. I do the work given to me right and on time. I even bring my work home. The way they speak hurts."), ("Speaker 1", "Hayaan mo na. May mga tao talagang utak talangka.", "Let it go. There really are crab-mentality people.")]
_L8 = [("Radio", "Congratulations kay Superintendent Defiesta, DENR ng National Capital Region, ang Bureau of Customs, Philippine Coast Guard at Naval Intelligence Special Forces.", "Congratulations to Superintendent Defiesta, the DENR of the National Capital Region, the Bureau of Customs, the Philippine Coast Guard and the Naval Intelligence Special Forces."), ("Radio", "Kahapon, dahil sa pinagsama-samang puwersa ng mga ahensiyang nabanggit, nasabat nila ang mga kahoy mula sa tatlong twenty-foot container van na naglalaman ng dalawampung libong board feet at tinatayang nagkakahalaga ng anim na raang libong piso.", "Yesterday, because of the combined forces of the agencies mentioned, they seized the logs from three twenty-foot container vans containing twenty thousand board feet and estimated to be worth six hundred thousand pesos. (The book’s key says 21,000 board feet; the script says 20,000.)"), ("Radio", "Galing Davao City ang mga ito.", "These came from Davao City."), ("Radio", "Nangako rin si Superintendent Defiesta at DENR na paiigtingin nila ang pagbabantay sa mga kagubatan para hindi na maulit ang malagim na flashflood na tumama sa Cagayan De Oro at Iligan City.", "Superintendent Defiesta and the DENR also promised to intensify the guarding of the forests so that the terrible flashflood that hit Cagayan De Oro and Iligan City will not happen again."), ("Radio", "Maganda ang layuning ito sana nga lang ay huwag maging ningas kugon at tuloy-tuloy na bantayan ang mga kabundukan.", "This purpose is good, but let us hope it will not be ningas kugon and the mountains will be guarded continuously.")]
_L9 = [("Speaker 1", "Ano, mag-aasawa ka na? Kaga-graduate mo lang ng college, wala ka pa ngang trabaho. At saka, mahirap maghanap ng trabaho sa panahon ngayon. E, ’yung mapapangasawa mo, meron ba siyang mapapakain sa ’yo? Ano bang natapos niya?", "What, you are getting married? You just graduated from college, you do not even have a job yet. And also, it is hard to find a job these days. And your future husband, does he have something to feed you with? What did he finish?"), ("Speaker 2", "High school graduate lang po siya. Pero, Tita, namamasada po siya. Tricycle driver po. Bahala na po. Ang importante nagmamahalan po kami. At saka, pakakasalan naman niya ako.", "He is only a high school graduate. But, Tita, he drives a tricycle for passengers. He is a tricycle driver. Bahala na. What is important is that we love each other. And besides, he will marry me."), ("Speaker 1", "Ano? Sherilyn naman, mag-isip-isip ka nga. Hindi puwedeng bahala na. Ang pag-aasawa, pinaplano nang mabuti, hindi idinadaan sa bahala na. Paano kung magka-anak kayo, ano ang ipapakain n’yo? Paano kung magkasakit kayo? Naku naman, Sherilyn.", "What? Sherilyn, think for a moment. Bahala na will not do. Marriage is planned carefully, it is not passed through bahala na. What if you have children, what will you feed them? What if you get sick? Goodness, Sherilyn.")]
